{"type":"click","text":"1\n      \n        Step progress bar\n        A row of labelled dots at the top — People · Scan · Review · Assign · Summary — so users always know where they are and how many steps remain. Tapping a completed step could also jump back to it.","choice":"progress-bar","id":null,"timestamp":1776999918869}
{"type":"click","text":"2\n      \n        Scan confidence hints\n        After scanning, flag items the AI was uncertain about with a subtle ⚠ icon in the Review step — so the user knows exactly what to double-check instead of eyeballing everything.","choice":"receipt-confidence","id":null,"timestamp":1776999920615}
{"type":"click","text":"3\n      \n        \"Split equally\" one-tap\n        A button in the Assign step that assigns every item to everyone with one tap — for groups that just want to go Dutch without thinking about it. Individual items can still be reassigned after.","choice":"split-equally","id":null,"timestamp":1776999922672}
{"type":"click","text":"4\n      \n        \"Everyone\" per-item shortcut\n        Each item card in Assign gets a small \"All\" pill alongside the person buttons. One tap assigns that item to the whole group — great for shared dishes like bread, apps, or a bottle of wine.","choice":"everyone-button","id":null,"timestamp":1776999926207}
{"type":"click","text":"9\n      \n        Summary celebration moment\n        A brief, tasteful animation when the Summary screen appears — gold confetti, a shimmer across the cards, or the totals counting up. Marks the satisfying end of the flow. Apps like Stripe and Duolingo nail this.","choice":"celebration","id":null,"timestamp":1777000012111}
{"type":"click","text":"8\n      \n        Step transitions\n        Smooth slide-in / slide-out animations when moving between steps — forward slides right, back slides left. Makes the flow feel like a real native app instead of pages popping in and out.","choice":"animations","id":null,"timestamp":1777000031200}
{"type":"click","text":"6\n      \n        Remembered names\n        The \"Who's splitting?\" step remembers names from past splits and surfaces them as quick-add chips. Start typing \"Gor\" and \"Gordon\" appears. Frequent groups form in seconds.","choice":"saved-names","id":null,"timestamp":1777000110978}
{"type":"click","text":"7\n      \n        Person colour coding\n        Each person auto-gets a warm accent colour (amber, rose, teal, etc.) that works with the dark theme. Their Assign pills, Summary cards, and breakdown rows carry their colour — making the whole split instantly scannable at a glance.","choice":"person-colors","id":null,"timestamp":1777000114719}
